<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="abstract1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Tiny Aya</span> redefines what a small multilingual language model can achieve.
Trained on 70 languages and refined through region-aware posttraining, it delivers state-of-the-art in translation quality, strong multilingual understanding, and high-quality target-language generation, all with just 3.35B parameters.
The release includes a pretrained foundation model, a globally balanced instruction-tuned variant, and three region-specialized models targeting languages from Africa, South Asia, Europe, Asia-Pacific, and West Asia.
This report details the training strategy, data composition, and comprehensive evaluation framework behind <span id="abstract1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Tiny Aya</span>, and presents an alternative scaling path for multilingual AI: one centered on efficiency, balanced performance across languages, and practical deployment.</p>
    
<p id="abstract1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="abstract1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Core Models</span></p>
    
<ul id="S0.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S0.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S0.I1.i1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\blacktriangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#2D4CB9;" mathcolor="#2D4CB9">▶</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\blacktriangleright</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<div id="S0.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
